WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:09.740
Deposit the cheques that are due in one go, then mark each one collected, or bounced if it comes back.

2
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:14.640
The portfolio lists the cheques you hold, the earliest due first.

3
00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:20.220
Cheques that are due are already ticked. Tick or untick any others.

4
00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:25.770
Under Deposit at the bank, choose the account and the deposit slip number.

5
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.610
Choose Deposit the ticked cheques.

6
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.540
They move to Deposited, waiting for the bank.

7
00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:45.740
When the bank clears one, open it.

8
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:54.400
Next step: mark it collected, and its invoice is paid. If it bounced, record that and the tenant is told.

9
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.100
This one cleared.

10
00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:04.600
The history keeps every step of the cheque, with who did it and when.
